{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>The purchase of the field, etc.</b> After he hinted to them the acquisition of the merit of the cave belonging to him alone, he returned to one particular detail that is subject to challenge regarding the cave — namely the sons of Heth, who can contest it by the law of bar metzra and remove it from their hands." "And although according to the law the right of the adjacent landowner (metzra) does not apply when purchasing from a gentile — this is only so if the one contesting is an Israelite, and the reason is as they said in the Talmud (Bava Metzi'a 108b): for he says to him, 'A lion tore [your acquisition] from your predecessor' — but in the situation before us this reason does not apply, and the gentiles will claim the law of the metzra to remove [the cave] from the hands of the sons of Jacob." "And relative to the claim of the metzra, it would not suffice that Abraham buried Sarah and Isaac [buried] Rebecca there, and so forth, as the Rambam wrote in chapter 13 of the Laws of Neighbors: whether [one] built or dug and caused damage, he is regarded as an agent, and [the owner] deducts from him if he caused damage." "Therefore he said <b>the purchase of the field</b> from the sons of Heth, so that they have no claim of bar metzra. And see what I have written in the portion of Chayei Sarah (Genesis 23:9)." "And the reason the verse did not arrange this particular [acquisition] immediately next to the purchase from Ephron is that his purchase from the sons of Heth is not in the same category and scope as his purchase from Ephron — for Ephron is the original owner from whose hand Abraham purchased, whereas the sons of Heth are merely a group among whom there is a basis for contest by the law of bar metzra. Therefore their words come at the end."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:51:15.364760290Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}